    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build passes. Only one test class exists (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are support classes (`AcceptanceBase`, `AuditLogCapture`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe de-duplication rule was specified in `CustomerCodes`/`AssignCustomerCode` but not actually implemented \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode` just set the raw computed code. I implemented the collision handling in `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\n- Computes the base code via `CustomerCodes.build(owner)` (unchanged `<REGION>-<HASH8>` identity).\n- Gathers every other owner's `customerCode` from `OwnerRepository.findAll()` (excluding the owner itself by id, matching the pattern used by `AssignNamesakeCount`).\n- If the base collides, appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and increments until the result is unique \u2014 so it correctly walks past `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 when earlier suffixes are also taken, yielding the smallest `n \u2265 2`.\n- Sets the resulting de-duplicated code on the owner.\n\nThe `OwnerRepository` is injected by type per OfficeFloor conventions, and the step still runs under `govern: [ transaction ]` in the existing `owners.POST.yml` pipeline. `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
